{"card":{"card_id":"ma-c-9f954d7d95f2f83fb2ed","statement":"In <<cite:2015arXiv150304817B>>, a monopole operator $M_{A,p}\\in\\CC[\\mathcal M_C]$ corresponding to a cocharacter $A$ and an $W_A$-invariant polynomial $p$ is considered. Here $W_A$ is the Weyl group of $\\Stab_G(A)$. Moreover a formula for the product $M_{A,p} M_{A',p'}$ is proposed. (See <<cite:2015arXiv150304817B>>.) They satisfy the triangular property, which is related to our filtration.\n\nTherefore $M_{A,p}$ could be related to our $f[\\cR_\\la]$ ($f\\in\n    \\CC[\\ft]^{W_\\la}$) under $A\\leftrightarrow \\la$, $p\\leftrightarrow\n    f$. However our $f[\\cR_\\la]$ lives in $\\gr\\cA$. It is not clear for us how to lift $f[\\cR_\\la]$ to $\\CC[\\mathcal M_C]$ canonically. Also it is not clear for us how to define the equivariant integration in <<cite:2015arXiv150304817B>> rigorously.","source_id":"arXiv:1601.03586","cluster":"representation_theory","statement_sha256":"c1b8639d55f66611b370a5c0644268767b70cc783cb887bac01f2b0bf95ca847","kind":"remark","label":"Remark 2","ref_key":"rem:BDG2","name":"","order":83,"deps":[],"cite_keys":["2015arXiv150304817B"],"provenance":{"source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1601.03586","harvest_mode":"arxiv_eprint","payload_sha256":"b2e79974e6e250f264382e70c5d3296d4abfc8d5c86da0ff1e8d9db5aafed33f","line":7700,"origin":"latex_env","retrieved_at":"2026-09-26T15:38:02+08:00"},"wash":{"version":"cardwash.v3","stages":["segment","purify","classify","dedupe","emit"],"numbering":"document_order_with_label_heuristic","detail":{"stripped_proof":false,"chars":780,"math_hints":58}}},"paper":{"source_id":"arXiv:1601.03586","title":"Towards a mathematical definition of Coulomb branches of $3$-dimensional $\\mathcal N=4$ gauge theories, II","abstract":"Consider the $3$-dimensional $\\mathcal N=4$ supersymmetric gauge theory associated with a compact Lie group $G_c$ and its quaternionic representation $\\mathbf M$. Physicists study its Coulomb branch, which is a noncompact hyper-Kähler manifold with an $\\mathrm{SU}(2)$-action, possibly with singularities. We give a mathematical definition of the Coulomb branch as an affine algebraic variety with $\\mathbb C^\\times$-action when $\\mathbf M$ is of a form $\\mathbf N\\oplus\\mathbf N^*$, as the second step of the proposal given in arXiv:1503.03676.","authors":["Alexander Braverman","Michael Finkelberg","Hiraku Nakajima"],"year":"2016","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1601.03586","cluster":"representation_theory","macros":{"RR":"{\\mathbb R}","bN":"\\mathbf N","SL":"\\operatorname{\\rm SL}","cO":"\\mathcal O","cal":"\\mathcal","Bbb":"\\mathbb","frak":"\\mathfrak","labelenumi":"\\textup{(\\theenumi)}","mathcal":"\\cal","mathbb":"\\Bbb","mathfrak":"\\frak","theenumi":"\\alph{enumi}","thmref":"\\ref{#1}","secref":"\\ref{#1}","lemref":"\\ref{#1}","propref":"\\ref{#1}","corref":"\\ref{#1}","subsecref":"\\ref{#1}","remref":"\\ref{#1}","defeq":"\\overset{\\operatorname{\\scriptstyle def.}}{=}","CC":"{\\mathbb C}","ZZ":"{\\mathbb Z}","QQ":"{\\mathbb Q}","proj":"{\\mathbb P}","CP":"\\proj","SU":"\\operatorname{\\rm SU}","GL":"\\operatorname{GL}","PGL":"\\operatorname{PGL}","U":"\\operatorname{\\rm U}","grpSp":"\\operatorname{\\rm Sp}","algsl":"\\operatorname{\\mathfrak{sl}}","su":"\\operatorname{\\mathfrak{su}}","gl":"\\operatorname{\\mathfrak{gl}}","g":"{\\mathfrak g}","Spec":"\\operatorname{Spec}\\nolimits","Proj":"\\operatorname{Proj}\\nolimits","End":"\\operatorname{End}","Hom":"\\operatorname{Hom}","Ker":"\\operatorname{Ker}","Coker":"\\operatorname{Coker}","Ima":"\\operatorname{Im}","dim":"\\mathop{\\text{\\rm dim}}\\nolimits","codim":"\\mathop{\\text{\\rm codim}}\\nolimits","rank":"\\operatorname{rank}","tr":"\\operatorname{tr}","id":"\\operatorname{id}","HH":"\\mathbb H","dslash":"/\\!\\!/","bM":"\\mathbf M","shfO":"\\mathcal O","la":"\\lambda","aff":"{\\operatorname{aff}}","Gr":"\\mathrm{Gr}","cR":"\\mathcal R","cF":"\\mathcal F","cT":"\\mathcal T","cK":"\\mathcal K","scP":"\\mathscr P","scA":"\\mat